[5] (RH) AND THE PIVOT-MAJORIZATION ROUTE  --  the measurement E05 needs
    DEFINITIONS USED, stated so the population cannot drift:
      pivots(pi) = the sequence of maxima removed by Havel-Hakimi, sorted decreasing.
      C1-X (ii): 2*sum(pivots(pi)) = sum(pi).
      unit transfer DOWN: pi' = pi - e_i + e_j with pi_i >= pi_j + 2.
        (Sec 7.55 (b) writes 'add 1 to an entry that is not larger'.  Taken literally
         that also admits pi_i = pi_j, which moves UP in dominance, and pi_i = pi_j+1,
         which is the identity as a multiset.  Only pi_i >= pi_j + 2 is a genuine
         down-move, and that is the definition used here.  Both looser readings are
         measured separately below so the discrepancy is on the record.)
      dominance a >= b for partitions of the SAME integer: every partial sum of a
        (sorted decreasing, zero-padded) is >= the corresponding partial sum of b.
   known-value  pivots([1,1,0,0])                        = (1,)           expect (1,)           OK
   known-value  2*sum(pivots) = sum, on (3,3,2,2,2,2,2)  = 0              expect 0              OK
   known-value  dominates((3,1),(2,2))                   = True           expect True           OK
   known-value  dominates((2,2),(3,1))                   = False          expect False          OK
   population: every partition pi of N in [2,16] whose HH run TERMINATES, and every
   pi' = pi - e_i + e_j with pi_i >= pi_j + 2 whose run also terminates.
   pairs in population: 1324.  Exclusions: lists whose run ABORTS -- skipped on BOTH
   sides and counted nowhere else.  N > 16 is OUT OF POPULATION and claimed nowhere.
   C1-X (ii) 2*sum(pivots) = sum : holds 209, fails 0
   (RH)  s(pi) <= s(pi')          : holds 1324, FAILS 0
   (PIVOT-MAJ)  p(pi) >= p(pi')   : holds 1324, FAILS 0 (first 0 printed)
   pivots() vs the DIFFED runA/runB step count: 0 disagreements
   loose reading pi_i == pi_j: 6986 such moves; of those, pi' DOMINATES pi (i.e. the move
   goes UP, not down) in 6986 -- which is why the definition above requires pi_i >= pi_j+2.
   CONTROL: the (RH) population is non-empty                          hits=1324     OK
   CONTROL: the loose reading pi_i == pi_j really does go UP (Sec 7.55 (b) imprecision) hits=6986     OK

